			<div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-[8px] p-[10px] shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
				<div>
					<div class="mb-4">
						<img src="/images/2026/01/QC1-copy.webp" width="1920" height="1024" alt="Interior Natural Light Analysis" class="w-full h-auto rounded-[8px] object-cover" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
					</div>
					<div class="p-2">
						<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">1. Interior Natural Light Analysis</h3>
						<p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
							Shadow Slice makes ceilings and upper walls transparent to the camera while keeping them completely solid to sunlight. This allows you to look inside and analyze realistic natural light distribution throughout the entire floor plan.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Case 2 -->
			<div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-[8px] p-[10px] shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
				<div>
					<div class="mb-4">
						<img src="/images/2026/01/QC2.webp" width="1920" height="1024" alt="Smart Section Compensation" class="w-full h-auto rounded-[8px] object-cover" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
					</div>
					<div class="p-2">
						<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">2. Smart Section Compensation</h3>
						<p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
							Traditional section planes let sunlight flood in from the cut plane, completely ruining interior shadow accuracy. Shadow Slice automatically compensates for the removed section, keeping shadow casting 100% physically accurate.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Case 3 -->
			<div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-[8px] p-[10px] shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
				<div>
					<div class="mb-4">
						<img src="/images/2026/01/QC3.webp" width="1920" height="1024" alt="Section-Based Shadow Studies" class="w-full h-auto rounded-[8px] object-cover" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
					</div>
					<div class="p-2">
						<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">3. Section-Based Shadow Studies</h3>
						<p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
							Analyze interior shadow behavior directly within longitudinal or transverse section views. Perfect for daylighting reports and client documentation.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Case 4 -->
			<div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-[8px] p-[10px] shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
				<div>
					<div class="mb-4">
						<img src="/images/2026/01/QC4.webp" width="1920" height="1024" alt="Perspective Cutaway Visualization" class="w-full h-auto rounded-[8px] object-cover" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
					</div>
					<div class="p-2">
