					<span>1. How is Shadow Slice different from native Section Plane?</span>
					<svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate-400 transition-transform duration-300 accordion-chevron flex-shrink-0 ml-2" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
				</summary>
				<div class="p-5 pt-0 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
					SketchUp’s native section cut removes geometry completely, allowing exterior sunlight to pour directly through the cut opening, which destroys realistic interior lighting. Shadow Slice makes the cut geometry invisible to your camera while retaining 100% of its shadow casting.
				</div>
			</details>

			<details class="group bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
